  "metadata": {
    "title": "Rothera: Robinhood’s Prediction Market Empire Is Quietly Taking Shape",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "-\nRobinhood's prediction market strategy is entering a new phase as it begins routing event contracts through Rothera, the regulated exchange it built with Susquehanna.\n-\nRothera could emerge as a major rival to Kalshi, with analysts warning that Robinhood's shift may divert a significant portion of trading volume away from the leading U.S. prediction market platform.\n-\nUnlike crypto-native Polymarket, Rothera is integrated into Robinhood's brokerage ecosystem.\nRobinhood Prediction Market:- Last year in November 2025, Robinhood announced a joint venture with Susquehanna International Group to build its own prediction market exchange. The move appeared to be an infrastructure investment rather than a major product launch.\nAt the time, the company said it would build a CFTC-licensed exchange and clearinghouse dedicated to futures, derivatives, and prediction markets.\nSix months later, that vision is now finally beginning to take shape through Rothera.\nJust last week, Robinhood started routing prediction-market products through Rothera. That's beginning with new World Cup event contracts and a revamped pricing model. What looked like a back-office acquisition is now finally becoming the foundation of Robinhood's next major growth engine.\nWhat Is Rothera?\nRothera, in simple words, is Robinhood's own prediction markets platform. It is the regulated exchange and clearinghouse that emerged from Robinhood's joint venture with Susquehanna.\nThe project was built through the acquisition of MIAXdx, a CFTC-licensed derivatives exchange. It gave Robinhood immediate access to the regulatory infrastructure required to operate prediction markets at scale. The acquisition closed in January 2026, giving the company control over a licensed marketplace rather than relying exclusively on external venues.\nIn practical terms, Rothera serves as the marketplace where event contracts can be listed, matched, and cleared.\nThis comes as Robinood's next big move after it launched AI crypto trading.\nHow Is Rothera Connected To Robinhood?\nRothera is not merely a partner platform.\nIt is effectively Robinhood's attempt to own the full prediction-market stack.\nUntil now, Robinhood's event contracts largely depended on outside infrastructure providers. By building Rothera, the brokerage gains greater control over product development. It can now do its own contract listings, liquidity, pricing, and the overall customer experience.\nJB Mackenzie, Robinhood's General Manager and Vice President of Futures and International said on the launch, \"It means better pricing for customers and a foundation for more innovative products down the road. Prediction markets are a growing and powerful financial tool, and we're excited for what's next.\"",
